# Qoder Sonus — findings by Claude Opus 4.6

- Source: Qoder / Bright Zenith (`qoder/sonus`)
- Date: 2026-11-04 (UTC)
- Overview and scoring methodology: `../../model-comparison.md`
- Cross-model signed log: `../../model-findings.md`

## Model card

- **Name:** Qoder Sonus
- **Short description:** Qoder's native SOTA-tier AI model designed for marathon-length autonomous agent workflows, heavy software engineering, and computer use. Deeply integrated with the Qoder ecosystem (Desktop IDE, CLI, JetBrains plugins, Cloud Agents) for end-to-end agentic engineering.
- **Provider / access:** Qoder platform (Desktop, CLI, QoderWake, Cloud Agents). Not available as a standalone public API. Credit-based billing.
- **Release / knowledge:** 2026; knowledge cutoff not publicly disclosed
- **IDs:** `qoder/sonus` (Qoder ecosystem only)
- **Context window:** Not publicly disclosed — designed for marathon multi-step execution
- **Modalities:** Text, image in (via computer use / desktop interaction); text out; tool calls yes; computer use yes (native desktop operation)
- **Pricing (as of 2026-11):** 3.2x credit multiplier within Qoder's paid tiers (Pro, Pro Plus plans with monthly credits). No standalone per-token pricing.
- **Architecture:** Proprietary closed-weight model; architecture details not publicly disclosed

